# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=open lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_wind
In 1972, a flight attendant fell from a height recorded as ten kilometres, with no parachute… and *lived*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=galley lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_ship_interior
Her name was Vesna Vulović, she was twenty-two, and she was not supposed to be on that *plane*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=badge lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_ship_interior
The airline had mixed her up with another stewardess, also named *Vesna*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=climb lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_wind
So on January the twenty-sixth, she took off from Copenhagen, bound for *home*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=windows lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_wind
There were twenty-eight people on *board*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=bomb lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_wind
Forty-six minutes later, a *bomb* went off in the baggage hold.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=break lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_wind
The plane broke into *three* pieces, over the snowy mountains of Czechoslovakia.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=pinned lead=.05 tail=.15 amb=real_wind
Vesna was in the tail, pinned to the floor by a food *cart*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=cart lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_wind
She did not know it yet, but that cart would *save* her life.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=faint lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_wind
As the air rushed out of the cabin, she passed *out*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=bp lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_wind
Doctors said her low blood pressure did that… and it kept her *heart* from bursting.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=fall lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_wind
Then the tail fell ten kilometres, towards a forest buried in *snow*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=impact lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_snow_wind
It came down among the trees, at just the right *angle*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=silence lead=.05 tail=.6 amb=real_snow_wind
Then, *silence*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=heard lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_snow_wind
A man from a nearby village heard someone *screaming* inside the wreck.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=honke lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_snow_wind
His name was Bruno Honke. In the war, he had been a *medic*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=aid lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_snow_wind
He found her under the cart, and gave her *first aid*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=alone lead=.05 tail=.45 amb=real_snow_wind
Of the twenty-eight people on board, she was the *only* one alive.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=injury lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_room_night
Her skull, her pelvis, both legs and three *vertebrae* were broken.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=coma lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_room_night
She lay in a coma for days, *paralysed* from the waist down.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=wake lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_room_night
When she woke, she remembered *nothing* of the crash, or the month after.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=walk lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_room_night
Ten months later, she *walked* again, with a limp she would keep for life.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=desk lead=.05 tail=.2 amb=real_room_night
She went back to the same airline, and worked at a *desk*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=record lead=.05 tail=.25 amb=real_wind
In 1985, Guinness named it the highest fall ever survived without a *parachute*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=medal lead=.05 tail=.3 amb=real_crowd
Her medal was presented by Paul *McCartney*.

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=cat lead=.05 tail=.35 amb=real_room_night
"I am like a *cat*," she later said. "I have had nine lives."

# vis kind=w act=x3_fall v=end lead=.1 tail=.9 amb=real_snow_wind
Her record still stands… and she never remembered a single *second* of the fall.
